// Quechua (qu) — Southern Quechua / Runasimi (Qhichwa; Cusco-Collao + Ayacucho), Latin script. Referee: the kaikki
// Quechua human set (English Wiktionary, 171 headwords after filtering loans/affix-stubs). Near-phonemic 3-vowel
// orthography with an overt 3-way stop series (plain / aspirated ⟨h⟩ / ejective ⟨'⟩). Wiktionary writes the phonemic
// /i u/ PHONETICALLY as [ɪ ʊ] and marks syllable dots + penultimate stress (both folded/stripped). epitran quy-Latn
// is an independent programmatic SECONDARY (fold-heavy — it emits English-ish lax [æ ɪ ʊ]). See
// docs/investigations/qu_native_bringup_investigation.md.
